<!--
  Doc 30 TASK-DESK-009. Tauri merges this file with its own auto-generated
  Info.plist (bundle identifier/version/category/minimum-OS-version are all
  already configured directly in tauri.conf.json's `identifier`/`version`/
  `bundle.category`/`bundle.macOS.minimumSystemVersion` fields -- no
  override needed here for any of those).

  Deliberately empty of CFBundleURLTypes: Document 30's own task text for
  this task describes registering a custom URL scheme
  (`dinero://oauth-callback`) for the OAuth PKCE redirect. That design is
  explicitly superseded -- Document 22 (Security & Authentication Design)
  §5 states plainly: "This is the authoritative, current design — the
  local loopback listener model — per Document 16 §7 and Document 21
  §2.1.2 ... [the deep-link callback] design is explicitly superseded and
  must not be implemented." The real, already-implemented OAuth flow
  (`ingestion::oauth`) binds a local `127.0.0.1:<ephemeral port>` HTTP
  listener instead (confirmed directly in that module's source), which
  needs no URL scheme, no Info.plist entry, and no entitlement at all.
  Recorded here, in the one place a future engineer would look for this
  exact omission, rather than silently leaving it unexplained.
-->
